57fp|n|The act of rising. ; A morning assembly or reception of visitors, -- in distinction from a soiree, or evening assembly; a matinee; hence, also, any general or somewhat miscellaneous gathering of guests, whether in the daytime or evening; as, the president's levee. ; An embankment to prevent inundation; as, the levees along the Mississippi; sometimes, the steep bank of a river.	V:139m,62,2~139m,62,2	N:136m,83,1;139m,75,5;afyi,60,3;2v4y,59,1~139m,75,5;afyi,60,3;2v4y,59,1;136m,83,1
